On 30 Sep 1998 14:36:10 -0700, TTK Ciar <billm@cygnus.com> wrote:

> There's a new faster speed that comes after "Ultra", but I'm not
> sure what it's being called.

Ultra2-wide, or just U2W for short.  It's 80MB/sec.  I believe the only
currently available cabling for it is 68-pin Low Voltage Differential
or LVD for short.  It has a 12 metre cable length limit so long as all
devices on the cable are LVD devices.  Reverts back to the regular Ultra
SCSI cable length limits (and slower 40 MB speed) if any devices on the
cable are not LVD.

I have an Adaptec AHA-2940-U2W SCSI controller with four Seagate
ST39102LW (9.1G 10K RPM Cheetah) drives on my Linux system.  Yes,
it's a screamer.

- Dan



