I've been using DEC equipment for nearly 20 years -- time flys when
 you're having fun. One of the things I'll miss most with the imminent
 passing of my last Alpha 3000-400 is the DEC round "hockey puck"
 mouse used for years on VAXstations and early Alpha workstations.
 What a great device (for those of us with large hands...) -- it
 has a fantastic "rotating peg" mechanism in place of the ubiquitous,
 but far inferior, "ball" mechanism. Works on almost any surface and
 never gets "dirty" or sticks.

 Does anyone know if this style of mouse has survived into the era
 of PS2-compatible rodents? Does anyone sell anything similar in
 shape and tracking mechanism for PC's? Is it possible to splice a
 modern connector onto the old DEC mice and get them it work with
 newer machines? Odd, I never thought I'd get misty eyed over a
 silly mouse....

                              Jay Ponder
                              ponder@dasher.wustl.edu



