Harald Volz wrote:
> 
> Dear colleagues,
> 
> at the moment I'm updating my machines from 3.2d to 4.0b
> I made a clean new installation on an external disk.
> After copying / and /usr via vdump / vrestore on the internal disk and
> changing fstab I'm booting from the internal disk.

Umm .. did I read that right?  You installed a new v4.0b system and
then dumped v3.2d copies of / and /usr on top of it?  If so, you have
just trashed your v4.0b install.  My advise -- start again, and this
time only (carefully) restore selected files, like /etc/passwd, /etc/hosts,
and other configuration (text) files from your old system.  Do not under
any circumstances replace any of the binary files.

