I just would like to disagree mildly about Volume Shadowing. As fas as
I know, it is actually so called "System Integrated Product". The
difference
between SIP and true "Layered Product" is that SIPs come preinstalled
with
VMS whilst Layered Prodcuts are installed after VMS is installed. Both
need license though usually. Typically SIPS had category E license
whilst
layered products had category F license. Of course, since Alpha things
have became more compicated as there are new license categories and some
things are not any included in VMS itself.

Most notably DECnet (Phase IV) used to true SIP but at V7.1 it actually
looks more of a true LAYERED PRODUCT.

Other SIPs are VMScluster and RMS journaling. And I would imagine that
GALAXY
is techinically a SIP as one only loads a license onto V7.2 system but
does not
install any software (in addition to VMS itself) in order to enable
galactic
operation.

Then again, maybe this SIP has been long since forgotten.

_veli




