I think you are in for a disappointment.  The closest you
might be able to find is that at onetime a company called
KiNet did support DS200s from Unix, but that was several
years ago, and the cost to buy their product far exceeds the
worth of a DS200.  Aside from the KiNET support, you would
also need the DS200 download image, available only from
Compaq, again costing far more than the DS200 is worth.

These terminal servers use MOP protocols to download a
control program, then communicate using the LAT protocols,
all proprietary to Compaq.  There is no TCP/IP support
whatsoever.  They are long obsolete, used only in VMS and a
few Digital Unix sites that still have the software to
support them.
