I have found that the CDE is not very robust in that if it cannot contact
as least one nameserver (in /etc/resolv.conf) it can choke and give very
misleading error messages. So this is a long shot but I would first check
if the network connection is working and that at least one nameserver
in /etc/resolv.conf is allowing name lookup. You could actually put
"nameserver 127.0.0.1" in /etc/resolv.conf to test. Silicon Graphics
workstations exhibit a similar behavior.

