I'm in the planning stage for a new system, and one of the options is an
internal 4mm DAT drive, a DEC TLZ09 (part number SN-TLZ09-LK), on the same
UltraSCSI bus as the system disk.  The new system will be one of DEC's Personal
Workstations.

Does anyone have any advice on the TLZ09 vis-a-vis a third party drive?  If the
TLZ09 has problems on newer systems with recent versions of VMS, I want to know
about it, but also I want to know if you've had a better experience with a
third party drive.

What about internal vs. external?  I figure I save a SCSI ID and a bit of cable
length by making it internal.

I currently use various third party drives, with varying degrees of success/
frustration, on various systems.  I use 120m tapes in all of them, and want to
continue using the same brand of tapes (Maxell) in the new drive.  Does anyone
know if Maxell has problems?  What about recycling 4mm tapes in a TLZ09 drive
that were originally written on other (non-DEC) DDS-2 drives?

Have there been problems reading TLZ09-written tapes on non-TLZ09 drives?  What
about the other way around?  Does it make a difference if compression is turned
on (I have it always on when writing)?

Thanks.

