The problem I've had with 4mm drives is that I all-too-frequently have to
power cycle the drives because they swallow a tape.  Internal tape drives
require power cycling the entire system.  That may not be a problem for a
workstation, but it's created problems with my server.  I would hope that
TLZ09's are more reliable than my older drives, but I have no experience
with them.  I also like external drives because I can move them around
if necessary.

