In article <6u82q7$21k$1@bunyip.cc.uq.edu.au>, "John Opitz" <flynnx@hotmail.com> writes:
:I just acquired two VAXStation 3100s and would like to know more about them.
:
:How do I find out the model number of each (as they are both different)? Is
:the model number written on the case?

  If it says "VAXstation 3100" on the front, then it is likely either a 
  model 30 (two horizontal rows of louvers on the side of the case) or a 
  model 40 (taller case, more internal storage, three rows of louvers on
  the side, but otherwise electronics are similar to the model 30.  Later 
  VAXstation 3100 series systems generally include the model number on
  the medallion on the front: the members include the 30 & 40 pair, and 
  the somewhat faster 38 & 48 pair, and the fastest of the series: 76.

  Look for the serial number sticker on the back of the system for the 
  serial number and model number.  The model number will probably be
  something akin to VS4xx for this particular system.

:One of the VAXs has a tape drive - what capacity tapes does it write?

  Probably a TZ30 DLT, with a capacity circa 90MB.  This tape drive uses
  the first-generation DLT media.  The TZ30 is a half-height tape drive, 
  with a horizontal lever across most of the width of the bottom of the 
  tape slot; the lever locks and unlocks the cassette.  If this is not
  it, then without a better description of what the drive looks like, it 
  may be difficult to specifically identify it.

:Given the model number, is there anywhere that I can get some benchmark
:information?

  Start with the OpenVMS FAQ, and the pointers to various websites that
  are included therein.  Also visit the newsgroup archives, as this and
  similar questions have been asked on various occasions in the past in 
  the comp.sys.dec and comp.os.vms newsgroups.

  The OpenVMS FAQ:

    http://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/dec-faq/vms

  Visit http://www.montagar.com/hobbyist/ for information on the DECUS
  hobbyist license.  (This hobbyist license for OpenVMS VAX V6.1 is 
  available in specific areas of the world.  I do not know the plans
  nor the availability of this license for your area.)

  Also check the SCSI system disk capacity limits for all members of
  the VAXstation 3100 series -- this is mentioned in the OpenVMS FAQ.

