but, all things being equal (i.e., nobodies changed instruction sets
significantly), the instruction rates should go up proportional to clock
frequency.

What gives? Did they really steal DEC's magic, and should the FTC be going
after them as they are? Or has Intel got really smart lately?

Rick (your average guy who designs BIPS machines and doesn't like everybody
to think it's that easy)





