I am having some problems with my digital Alphastation 255 running OSF
3.2. The system usually runs xdm to handle login and X. However,
recently the X server died and did not come back on. I altered the
Xserver line in the xdm setup to get as much info as possible about any
error. The stumbling block seems to be explained in the following error
message;

--v--v--
Workstation device failure.
Cannot find loadable library to handle device ZLXp2-EV4.
Could not AddScreen, ID = ZLXp2-EV4

Fatal server error:
no screens found
--^--^--

An output of the loaded libraries showes the following for what I
assume are the possible video cards:
--v--v--
   Library Name Library File Na       Init Proc Name DeviceName
       _dec_vga  lib_dec_vga.so        vgaScreenInit     (null)
    _dec_triton lib_dec_triton.  pwgaScreenInit_base    QVision
     _dec_ati64 lib_dec_ati64.s   atiScreenInit_base      ATI64
     _dec_ati32 lib_dec_ati32.s ati32ScreenInit_base      ATI32
--^--^--

Now, I have done some reading and the ZLXp2-EV4 is either the Screen
Device or the Video card. However, since I have not changed these or
anything else since the last time Modal was rebooted and the libraries
appear to be loaded I do not know what the problem is.

What I have tried so far:
I have tried restarting xdm, changing run level to 2 and back to 3.
I have tried both warm and cold boots.
I have fsck'ed '/' and '/usr' and they have come up clean.
