	Welcome to VAX/Linux. :)  A small group of us are working on porting 
 Linux to the VAX once again, since the original project has stalled. 
 Unfortunetly, we need some equipment, and right now, (speaking for myself),
 I barely have money to eat. 
 
        I know there must be people out there with VAX 6000 clusters or other
 large equipment that is being replaced with Alpha systems or NT.  It's a 
 sad situation, but it happens every day.  If you are in the south-eastern
 United States, we would probably be willing to come pick up this equipment 
 for you.  If you have any systems you are willing to donate - anything at
 all - please contact us.  Currently, the baseline would be a VAXstation 
 2000 with Ethernet, 8MB of RAM, and a RD54.  We are actively seeking 
 VAXstation 3100's, and VAX 4000, 6000, and 9000 systems if possible.  Anyone
 selling such systems, please contact us and we may be able to work out 
 something.  Even an 11/780 may be useful to us if it's close by, so please
 mail us!  For more information on the project (and there isn't much now, but,
 now is coming soon) please check out http://www.trn.nu.  There will be more
 information available soon. (Parts are helpful too... especially RD drives,
 since they tend to be expensive to replace via DEC and die rather easily).

	Any systems we have will be publicly available for developers who are
 actively involved in the project for any work they might need to do.  We
 really need someone who has low-level coding experience on these CPU's, since
 our experience hasn't covered this architecture.  We also need some VMS
 experts here and there, and generally any VAX guru interested in the project.
 It's going to be a real adventure, and we need all the help we can get.

 Thanks alot!

