I have no doubt that I could spend a chunk of time to duplicate what SCO
5.0.4 does. That's not the point. The point is that the emulation in
SCO OpenServer is much more complete than even Unixware's, and the reason
is that it's using Microsoft's code from Xenix.

Why would they spend the time and effort to duplicate the obscure edges
of the Xenix emulation when they have the code in-house already? So up
through Unixware 7 and Open Server 5.0.4, there's still Xenix code in SCO.
They have reached an agreement with Microsoft, so future versions won't
include that particular code... so maybe I'll be working on the iBCS
emulation after all. But right now, System V on the Intel platform
still has Xenix in its heritage.

That's the point... we're talking about the OS geneology, not which OS is
better.

