> All:
> I have 3 6XXX systems, each with a DSSI controller and an HSC.  We
> currently use TF867s for backup.  The loaders on these things are
> terrible and field service is equally bad fixing them.
> 
> I'd like to replace them with a single higher capacity DLT, something
> with the equivalent capacity on a single tape.  I realize I will
> probably have to add a SCSI controller to the system, but that's not an
> issue.   Any recommendations on Brand/Model/things to watch out for ??

The TZ89 has a capacity of 35gb native and 70gb compressed.  You
might want to consider the TL891.  It's a 10 tape mini-library
with one or two TZ89's.  We've got several of them and they seem better
than the TF8x7 type loaders.  

