You just renumber the system call when you expand its argument.  The program
may appear to be making the same system call, but the stub in libc has a new
system call number, and that system call in the kernel returns the new
data type.  It's not so painful.  You retain the old system call with the old
number so that old binaries continue to work -- if the user's built his
kernel with that kind of backwards compatibility turned on, usually.

