>Does anyone know how to make a DEC Alpha
>behave like an Intel Pentium in numerical calculation.

>I tried to use the egcs 1.0.3 C-Compiler on both machines.
>But the results are still different.

	Are there switches to force IEEE-format on both platforms?  Native
Intel (internal) format uses 80-bit numbers while the Alpha is limited to
64-bit, so if the Pentium code is able to keep intermediate code on the
FP stack (or stores temporaries in the 80-bit format) then the results may
well diverge.

