This is really an NFS version 3 problem.

I tested this between a 2.7 (largefile) system and a 2.5 system.
The 2.5 system complained that it couldn't decode the RPC-result:

NFS readdir+ failed for server host:name error 2 (RPC: Can't decode result)

Comment from bugid 1245104:
--------
This is not a bug.  Solaris 2.5 was modified to do this purposefully.  Previous
versions of Solaris did not know anything about largefiles and apparently the
other vendor's platform was returning the maximum file size through the
NFS Version 2 protocol instead of the correct size or an error.  This is why
access through NFS Version 2 appeared to work.  It wasn't working correctly.
