In article <36062A0E.3494F2D4@ave.ac.agit.de>, Roland Ziegler <zi@ave.ac.agit.de> writes:
|>Can a VAX 4000-200 be upgraded?
|>
|>The 4000-200 has a KA660 CPU module, with on-board DSSI controller,
|>Ethernet and memory controller and is mounted in a BA 215 box.
|>
|>I would prefer to keep the system box and just swap the CPU module (and
|>maybe the memory boards) to a newer 4000 model.

The VAX 4000-200 is more a member of the MicroVAX 3000 series than the
VAX 4000 series. All the other VAX 4000s (except the VAX 4000-10x) live
in the same sort of cabs (BA4xx). The VAX 4000-200 was really a drop in upgrade
for the MicroVAX 3600/3900 machines with the added benefit of on-board
DSSI.

There is no further upgrade - unless you can get hold of the very rare 
KA50 VAXbrick (but I know very little about those other than the fact that
they existed and may have been sold as the VAX 4000-50).

Antonio

