You're correct.  Thank you for clearing that up.  However, I have yet to
see a program to clean /tmp that is not vulnerable to race conditions. 
The only idea that I have come up with: setting job priority to
Real-Time, doing the check & rm, then going back to regular priority,
has a severe flaw if /tmp is NFS-mounted, and the NFS server goes down,
then the system will completely freeze.  Of course, you would have to be
an idiot to put /tmp on NFS, but I've seen worse.



