If you have write access to a directory outside /tmp you don't need to
perform this sort of shenanigan, and in any case the test will have
already failed. If you don't, and you're in /etc still, all that will
happen is that the bogus symbolic link will be deleted.

You can add an extra set of suspenders. I don't know whether this test
is actually useful, but:

>> >>       cd "$d"
>> >>       if [ "`pwd`" = "$d" ]
>> >>       then
              case ".$d" in
		./tmp*) rm "$f";;
	      esac
>> >>       fi

