Lodovico,

Non e' possible di montare una processore MMX nella Venturis FE 5120.

The Venturis FE 5120 will not work correctly with an MMX processor due
to differences between core voltage of the processor and core voltage
supported by the motherboard.

A Pentium MMX OverDrive should work properly, because it is designed
with the same core voltage as the Pentium 120 currently in your
system.

Also, you should be able to change a jumper on the motheboard to boost
the clock speed from its present 60 MHz to 66 MHz.

Finally, I have not tried either a Pentium MMX with a PowerLeap
adapter or a non-Intel processor.  The best non-Intel processor to try
is the IDT C6 WinChip, which operates at the same core voltage as the
Pentium 120, and runs at a maximum speed of 240 Mhz.  I would also
recommend a cooling fan mounted on the WinChip.  

I have tested the WinChip in several other DEC personal computers with
Phoenix BIOS, and it seems to run OK.  A little slow on floating point
though... Ben Myers

