Thomas Tornblom wrote:
> "Rev. Don Kool" <oldno7@home.com> writes:

> >       Yes, you can increase your swap space and take advantage of the
> > fact that SUN oddly uses that for "/tmp".  If "/tmp" is on a regular
> > UFS partition however, you're out of luck.

> Why is that "oddly"? 

	Because no one else does it that way.  That makes it odd.

> It has several advantages, like being blindingly
> fast on a machine with large amounts of RAM?

	And grinding your machine to a halt if it doesn't.  RAM is still
quite a bit more expensive than hard disk space even these days.

