> See? I growed the filesystem while it was still mounted.

	Interesting.  How quaint that you had to stay on the same disk to
do it.  Lucky for you that disk had a free partition/slice. 

> IMO have you not been able to show *anything* of your "Sun deficiency".

	IMO you have not been able to show that SUN is even capable of
producing a keyboard with the keys in the correct position.  One
would think that after all these years even SUN would figure out
that "caps lock" goes above "shift", not below it.  Perhaps no one
at the company has ever seen a typewriter.  Either that or they all
type with two fingers like most of their users.

> I can very well understand that you are frustrated with Sun:s. Things
