like SNI or NCR what would you prefer. An OS 
that has actually got x86 apps ported to it 
and has been proven to scale on very large 
machines, or an OS like HP-UX or DU which has 
never run on intel boxes, has no x86 apps 
ported to it and has never run on boxes bigger 
than 16 or 10 CPU's. 

One of Gartners greatest reservations about 
Merced is their concern that many existing 
x86 applications vendors will not bother to 
