"Rev. Don Kool" <oldno7@home.com> writes:

> 	I usually run a "find" and have it remove everything with an
> "atime" over 7 days.  If that doesn't clear enough, I increase the
> size of "/tmp".  (Ooops... that's right... can't do that on a SUN
> while it's running.  Thanks SUN!)

Yes you can. Just create an extra swap file (or dig out an extra
partition somewhere) and do "swap -a file" (where file is the file
name or device name).

The reason for this is that /tmp is in effect a RAM disk, so it takes
its space from the virtual memory.

And yes, you can remove the "swap" line from /etc/vfstab and use /tmp
just like any other Unix.

-- 
