:I'm looking for examples or pointers in writing an authentication module to
:be used in place of the sys$share:pwrk$acme_module.exe to work with other
:forms of authentication (eg LDAP and Radius). Any contributions welcome.

  The OpenVMS Ask The Wizard area will have an answer for this question
  within the normal turn-around time -- by some fluke, almost the very 
  same question was recently answered by the OpenVMS Wizard -- but you 
  likely already guessed that. :-)

  There is no external documentation on this interface, and support and
  documentation of sys$acme_module is not expected to be included with 
  the V7.2 release.  Once the nuances of the interface have shaken out,
  then documentation and support will likely be made available.  

  OpenVMS Engineering is already directly aware of your organization's 
  interest in this particular interface, and I suspect that this entire
  discussion would best be worked offline...  And if you do not already
  have any contacts, then send me your request for assistance directly 
  and I will forward it along to the OpenVMS security product manager.

