	We haven't had too much trouble with them other than what I
described.  We used to have a lot of trouble with IBM disks that SGI
used to use.  We had a Challenge that used to get disk failures
every time it was powered down.  According to the SGI hardware tech,
the solution was to pull the disk out and bang it on the floor to
free the heads!  It worked great for a long time.  Eventually some
would get so stuck that no manner of banging (even really hard
banging) would bring them around.  It did provide for some amusement
and venting of frustrations though.  At that time the 2GB disks were
going fro around $1800/ea and we eventually had SGI come in and
replace about 18 of them for free.  Never had a problem since.

	BTW; we tried banging the Quantums but they wouldn't come around. 
I have had this technique work great on other drives though.  Since
they're stuck anyway, there isn't much to lose (but your data!) so
it's generally worth a try.


