> >for any kind of time up record on my systems.  Longest uninterrupted
> >stretch of uptime is not what interests my users.  Highest
> >percentage of usable uptime during their shift is.

> Do you ever check to see if your users are running a long job that may take
> hours to complete?

	They don't do that on the workstations.  On the rare occassion that
a user does something like that, they do it on the servers.  Most of
our workstations get used like glorified PCs.  Users run Netscape,
FRAMEMAKER, e-mail and some applications specific to our Agency. 
When five o'clock hits, they log out and go home.  Then their
workstations are mine for the taking.

