Oh my god, you have to re-build the kernel to support 
real time on DU. How very primative. The Solaris 
scheduler supports fixed priority scheduling and 
the kernel fully supports kernel pre-emption. You 
can also lock down memory etc. You can turn 
pre-emption off but you don't need to re-build 
anything to do this. Solaris fully supports the 
POSIX.1.b real time extensions and the POSIX.1.c 
threads interface both of which are applicable to 
RT.

No Sun does not include a C compiler though we 
do include the headers, make, assembler etc. You 
can of course use gcc or for the price of a PWS 600 
you can get a Ultra60 and a very nice ANSI C/C++ 
Compiler and development environment.


