me check on one file - about 90MB long when it should be 10 MB.
He said that was the sign that the application hadn't been shut
down manually - so he spent the next 2 to 3 hours fixing some of
the corrupiton - and they only lost 2 days or orders.  :-(

Fifteen years ago you'd see corruption on Unix files systems - but
probably only 1 in 100 crashes (just what I've noticed - so thats
not a true statemnet of facts - just what I've observed)

Hard drive failure is the major problem in today's world - and that
is getting more rare.


