Well the best and biggest Alpha workstation when compared 
with the best and biggest Sun workstation. This is currently 
the Sun Ultra 60 360 Mhz and the AlphaStation 600 with 
600 Mhz 21164.

                 Sun Ultra60   Digital PWS 600
SPECint95        16.1 (1 cpu)  18.4
SPECfp95         23.5 (1 cpu)  21.3
CPU's	         2             1
SPECrate_int95   287 (2 cpus)  165
SPECrate_fp95    382 (2 cpus)  191

Graphics Benchmarks
ViewPerf CDRS-03 133 (1 cpu)   60
         DX-03   25.6(1 cpu)   13.8

Expansion
Maximum memory   2 GB          1.5 GB
PCI              66 Mhz/64bit  33 Mhz/64bit
		+66 Mhz/32bit +ISA
Graphics ports   2 x UPA       None uses PCI	  
UltraSCSI        Two Standard  Standard
100baseT         Standard      Standard

So exept for SPECint the fastest current single 
CPU Alpha workstation is slower on every measure, 
both CPU and graphics than the fastest single CPU 
Ultra. While being less expandible 

The Sun has a much faster Graphics bus, 
120 Mhz/128 bit UPA rather than 33 Mhz/64 
bit PCI and has more faster bus slots. 

Yes you can get faster Alphas, but not in 
workstations the 8400/4100 are hardly desktop 
machines.

These are of course SPEC benchmarks and you 
may counter with Alpha having faster application 
performance, again this is not so. 

One v large American Car manufacturer holds regular
application performance benchmark trials with all 
their workstation apps for all the major vendors. 

2D, 3D, FE etc etc Digital have never won this 
competition and in the last trial did not even 
bother to enter. Previous results had been to 
my recollection, 2and, last, last. 

These benchmarks were run as far back as Suns 
first Ultra workstations being introduced in 
1995. All this time Digital has claimed some 
sort of magical performance lead for Alpha. 

Finally the PWS 600 with PowerStorm 4D/60T 
128 MB RAM, 4.3 GB drive, 21 inch display
is 20% more expensive than an Ultra 60/360 
with the Elite M6 Graphics 256 MB and a 
9.1 GB drive. With a dual CPU Ultra 60 
being approx the same price as a single 
CPU PWS 600. 

