Sorry, not even Sun writes perfect operating system code.  Sometimes a
reboot is the only solution.

As an example, about two months ago, none of my Solaris 2.5.1/2.6 users
could read their email.  I was still running 1.1.1 at the time on my
workstation, so I didn't notice it until it was reported to me.

Something had gone horribly wrong with email locking on our server.  Running
truss for any user on any 2.x system showed the process hanging at a system
call.  The system even took a long time to respond to a "kill -9" of the
mail process.

The easiest solution was to reboot our server, and Enterprise 3000 (2.6).
Sure enough, that fixed the problem.  I've never see the problem seince then.

I checked the Sun bugs data base, and sure enough the problem has been seen
as far back as 2.2, and as recent as 2.6.  There aren't any solutions, as
the problem can't be repeated.

