put less money into R&D, less money into innovative architectures and
ultimately most of the diversity of platforms that was once a feature of
the computing world and one of the great early boosts for UNIX growth, has
been obliterated, only to remain in a few small niches and a few remaining
installations (im quite sure there are hundreds of Symmetrys still
out there running real-world work, and even probably a couple Molecular's, 
for that matter, among others!) 

alas that the wintel marketing juggernaut, aided by tens of millions of
clueless home users, has destroyed the engineering excellence and
innovation that was once part and parcel of the industry! 

