Australian sited TA/TU78's were single phase, 240VAC and WILL run off a
heavy duty domestic (2+hp Airconditioner type) 15A outlet
if you remove the gigantic 3 phase plug (cabled for one phase only) and
replace it with a 3 pin mains plug.
It tends to blow the fuse on a standard domestic 10 amp wall socket when the
compressor fires up. (No surprise there)
It actually pulls about 8 amps or so but the compressor startup (when you
load a tape) pulls just over 15, dropping back to around 10-12 once it's
running.
You could cheat and stick 15amp fuse wire in a 10 amp circuit and it might
work ok.
Domestic wiring (here) has about a 50% safety factor, so it would be good
for at least 15amps anyway without getting hot.
(But I don't recommend it.)

I still have one complete TA78 with it's TU78 slave deck, (That I'd like to
use, believe it or not)
but a 2 of the 5v P/S are crook beyond repair and I haven't been able to
find any (affordable) replacements. (Yet)

