In article <35FD3EEA.D3BF7F9@localhost.localdomain>,
root@localhost.localdomain (Remco Post) wrote:


> I have this rz58-e sitting around here, and I'd like to put it to use. I
> was told that it is a SCSI disk, with an extra (storageworks?) connector
> next to the SCSI connector. Can I use this connector easily to set the
> SCSI address of the disk, and if so, how? I couldn't find any info on
> this disk on the net, othar than it being replaced in digitals product
> portfolio some years back.

 Hello Remco,
 
  The RZ58-E is a 1.3GB SCSI drive, the connector next to the SCSI
  connector contains the SCSI ID select pins, and the 'spin on power
  up' option pin.
 
 
    :::::::::::::::::::::::::  ::::::::::::::
 
       50-pin SCSI conn.       123S
                                  P
                                  I
                                  N
 
     The SCSI ID pins '123' require a jumper 'IN' for a '1'
     The Spin On Power Up option jumper requires to be IN
     for the RZ58-E to spin on powerup.
 
 
     Hope this helps,
 
     Brian
 
     brobson@cix.compulink.co.uk
 






