>my first PC and I've just gotten the upgrades since then rather than
>switch to Quicken.)  I know that every time a new version of "Money"
>comes out, it reads the older file format.

I'll bet it doesn't write it. If you needed to interoperate (as we do) then
you'd be dealing with a whole other problem.

>> That's me. You prefer walking across the building every time some user's
>> got a configuration problem? Or you prefer talking them through it?

