  That's an internal part number. There's a "model number" like "F880" or
"M990" as well. The most common of these is the F880, which comes in both
a 1600BPI-only and a 1600/3200 dual density unit.

  Most of these are formatted Pertec interface drives. The DEC M7454 (TU80
controller) or its Dilog equivalent (DU130/DU132) will run this drive. How-
ever, this is a rather strange streaming drive in that the OS device driver
needs to tell the drive whether to stream (at high speed) or not. So you
may only get low-speed operation out of it.

