> |> "pseudo-Unix" comment come from with respect to Solaris x86?

> |       I would never consider SUN SOLARIS to be UNIX.  It is merely a
> |varaint.  As is "Solaris x86".

> Then what is "Unix"?

	UNIX is a general term that describes the basic way of doing things
that all the OSs have in common.  Like "car" or "truck".  They all
have easily recognizable traits that make them "a car" or "a
truck".  There is no 'standard issue, one each' "car" and there is
no 'standard issue, one each' "UNIX".  SOLARIS is not UNIX, it's a
unix.  One of many.

			Hope this helps,
			      Don


