Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


We got an AlphaStation 433au (Digital Unix Specified). It arrived and
I powered it up and got, not the SRM console, but some crappy firmware
which called itself the AlphaBIOS. It "announced" that there was no
WIndows NT Kernel on the disks, which is not surprising since the
one drive has Digital Unix 4.0D on it. Not to worry, on page 3-28 it
says to simply press F2 for the AlphaBIOS Setup, choose "CMOS setup",
press F6 for "Advanced setup", and select "Digital Unix"; then power
of, wait at least 45 seconds and power up (to the SRM). I did this
and it came right back to the sleazy pair: AlphaBIOS+WindowsNT.

Thinking that the SRM firmware was out of date or corruped, I used
the Firmare CD which comes with Digital Unix 4.0D to "re-burn"
all the firmware, and this verified. 

It didn't help.

I downloaded the LATEST firmware from Compac (aka Dec) and did
the same thing

It didn't help.

I thought that the motherboard might be strapped to prevent Firmware
update but on changing a few non-controversial CMOS values and
cycling these new values did hold - the only thing which doesn't
hold it the "Choice of Operating System".

At this point I don't have anymore ideas. Has anyone out there
seen this type of problem? Thanks,

