skrass@my-dejanews.com writes:

>Hi,
>Setting up an old Vax Station 4000 VLC.  I need to get an external SCSI CDROM
>that OpenVMS will be happy with.  Any suggestions?
>Thanks,
>Spencer

You need a CDROM that supports 512 byte sectors.  The standard PC spec
uses 2048 byte sectors.  Many "PC" CDROMS support 512 byte sectors either
via jumper or under software control, but it's not an advertized spec.

onsale.com sells DEC RRD45s under the name 'Toshiba 5401B 4X CD ROM' for
$27.00, if you don't mind the slow (by today's standards) speed (4x).

-Mike



