ew@spam.free.mail wrote:
> 
> Hey,
> 
>         Not that I am huge fan of glittery GUIs - but having multiple terminal
> sessions is a big plus... can I run Decwindows on VMS 5.4 Vaxserver 3200,
> 16 mb?  I don't believe I have any graphic hardware currently, so if this is
> even possible I will need a graphics card (uh... module?) and a tube that
> will display to the correct spec.  Ideas ?  If this is possible, where would
> I find the Decwindows Code ?

Yes, it is possible.  If you put graphics in a VAXserver 3200, it is
called a VAXstation 3200.  Unfortunately, I think that will change your
VMS licensing requirements and your VMS PAKs will probably not work
anymore.

Your best bet might be to upgrade to VMS V5.5-2 and get the hobbiest
license.  Check out:

	http://www.montagar.com/hobbyist/index.html

This would give you VMS 5.5-2 and DECwindows 5.5.  (Or VMS 6.1)

You also need a graphics board.  A VCB02 is one possibility.  With this
you can drive a VR290 type monitor at 1024x864 with up to 256 colors. 
16MB is on the light side.  You might also want to add another memory
board.  Unfortunately, all of these boards can fill up your 3200 pretty
fast.  You will need to see home much space you have available inside
your machine.

Good luck!

