skrass@my-dejanews.com writes:
> Setting up an old Vax Station 4000 VLC.  I need to get an external SCSI CDROM
> that OpenVMS will be happy with.  Any suggestions?

  You need a drive that can be set to the non-standard (for CD-ROMs) sector 
size of 512 bytes.

  DEC's RRD4x series comes this way (of course 8-). The current drive is the
RRD47, with a list price (for internal versions) of $330. This is a 32x drive.
The RRD46, a 12x drive, is also available (for a limited time) but it's the
same price.

  The Plextor UltraPlex drive is also a 32x drive and has a jumperable 512
byte option. It lists "DEC VAX" as one of the supported systems. List price
on the 32Tsi (internal model, tray loading) is $189. PC Connection has it for
$179, and you should be able to find it at most quality mail-order dealers.
I'm using one of these on one of the Onsale Alphastation 200 4/233 systems and
it works quite well.

  You could also buy a used RRD42 drive from a DEC reseller. External units
seem to be selling for $30-$150, depending on the phase of the moon.

