In article <6stun5$rro$1@Nntp1.mcs.net>,
  rer@mcs.net (Richard E. Robbins) wrote:
> I'd like to connect a VT420 to the serial port of a Sparc Station LX and I'm
> not sure which variant of the H8571 adapter to use?

The Sun is a DTE (computer as opposed to modem) device with 25-way female
connector(s), so in theory you should be using an H8751-C.

Although I've got a SPARC and a VT420 in front of me at the moment, I
can't find my H8571-C connector, so I've used an H8571-A with a 25M-25M gender
changer. That configuration works OK because AFAIK the only difference
between the -A and -C is the gender.

You may like to check this in Richard Shuford's terminal archive;
specifically, the DEC connector news at:

http://www.cs.utk.edu/%7Eshuford/terminal/dec_connector_news.txt

Take this with a pinch of salt though: it claims that there are only
four MMJ-DB25 adaptors but leaves out the H8571-A.

HTH,
Paul

