  Ken Hansen <khansen@pluto.njcc.com> wrote:
> What is the H8571? I simply took a null-modem adapter and started
> the system up... is that a Sun serial adaper to allow you to use
> both serial ports? I simply used the A port and ignored the B port,
> since it is placed on otherwise "unused" pins of the connector...

It sounds like you're lucky enough to have a VT420 with a DB25
connector on the back, which (I think) would be a European model.
Certainly this kind of question came up here regarding a VT320
some time back and some of us Europeans were surprised to hear
that US VT320s only had MMJ connectors and no DB25.

H8571 and H8575 is the family name for connectors which convert
MMJ to either DB25 or DB9.

