MMJ are a class of connectors, of which the RJ45 is an example. 
In this case, the MMJ connector on the majority of VT[34][24]0s is
the same size as an RJ45 and has the same auantity of pins, but the
locking tab is offset to one side, as opposed to the RJ45's centered tab. 
One can easily make a connector and adapter for these cjacks by breaking
the tab off of an RJ45 connetor and wiring the lines on the other end of the cable to 
a DB25 connector. 
The DEC-423 , one should note, is a differential interface, and so you need to
connect the returns on the 423 side to the ground on the RS232 side. 


happy hacking,
gregg
