But HSCs are such fun! Anyway, changing between KA62A, KA62B and KA64A is
more or less plug and play. Moving up to the KA65A or KA66A requires either
a backplane upgrade or a T2019 XREG module to provide a voltage that those
CPUs need. You also need to upgrade the memory from MS62 to MS65 (although
those are I, believe, backwards compatible with the older CPUs so swapping
back, should you need to do so, is less work). You also need to consider
upgrading any T2012 (XMI to BI) adapters to T2018 (XMI+ to BI).

