I have a scratch VAX with RZ24 only, that I managed to upgrade it to VMS 7.1
by some pruning. It has UCX 4.1 and FMS runtime loaded also. There is no
way I could get DECNET Plus on that disk, I tried tailoring off all DECWindows
(even base support) and uninstalling Phase IV DEcnet. Shame, I wanted to play
with DECnet over IP.

Of course, VMS 5.x does fit quite nicely onto a RD54 (no thought of OSI or UCX then).
If you have a GPX and the VWS kit installed then the graphics is quite fast. I don't
think I ever dared load up the DECWindows workstation support and set WINDOW_SYSTEM
= 1 on one of those boxes. Probably 6.2 should be OK too.


