Not sure about the RD54, I never saw any of those in external cabinets, but you can
get3rd party QBus SCSI controllers. If you really wanted too. These were great boxes
in their
time, just ran and ran and ran, but really what would you do with those many GB of
data on
a .9 VUP machine? Put the data on a more recent, faster box with built in SCSI and
access
it via the cluster (if you are lucky and have appropriate NAS or VMSCLuster
licences) or NFS.

Good luck
