In article <35f66f10.707697@news.mindspring.com>, tom@automatedtech.com (Tom Hickerson) writes:
>My WANrouters are going to be replaced with CISCO routers configured 
|>to route TCP/IP only.  If all three of my sites are in DECnet area 1
|>and only one system at each of the sites has TCP/IP, can I configure
|>that system as a routing DECnet node so that I can reach the other
|>DECnet modes at each site transparently ?

I think you are out of luck here. Applications on your DECnet-Plus end nodes
that have UCX should be able to reach other similarly configured nodes anywhere
in the network, but other nodes (i.e. those missing either DECnet-Plus or
a suitable IP transport) will not be able to talk to each other.

The DECnet-over-IP stuff doesn't do Routing too, as far as I can see.

Antonio

