>>
>> Are there any keyboard/video switches that will handle DEC terminals??

How about an electronic switch? eg Decserver 200/300/700/...
Create password-protected Reverse-LAT services on the Decserver and 
configure the ports going to the machine consoles as a "printer"(not terminal)
Then you can put the physical terminal onto one of the other ports(terminal 
configuration) and CONNECT to the appropriate LAT service.(you could also 
use a VMS workstation Decterm window to SET HOST/LAT also)

At one stage I used a Decserver300 to control the consoles for an RA81, a 
PDP11, 2 VAXes, 3 Translan bridges and a couple of Decmux2 consoles, using
this setup , when I only had one physical terminal and a Vaxstation2000
running VWS for my extra terminal connections.(in a "perfect" world I would
have liked a Decsever700 with boot from Flash Rom to overcome the MOP
download requirement, should this have become an isolated network, which
thankfully it wasn't and thus didn't result in the chicken & egg syndrome) 

