Hello,

I came over a problem with cxx which puzzles me a bit.  Consider the 
following C++ file:

-----bug2.C----------------------------------
struct Bar {
  int foo;
};

template < class T > void foo(T t);

void baz () {
  Bar bar;
  bar.foo = 10;
  if (bar.foo < 0)
          bar.foo = -bar.foo;
}
---------------------------------------------

While gcc 2.7.2 accepts it without problem, cxx spits:

fantomas: cxx -c bug2.C
cxx: Error: bug2.C, line 10: expected a ">"
  if (bar.foo < 0)
-----------------^
cxx: Error: bug2.C, line 10: explicit function template argument lists are not supported yet in expression
          contexts
  if (bar.foo < 0)
----------^
2 errors detected in the compilation of "bug2.C".


It seems that it mixes the template function foo() with the Bar struct 
member foo. Is that a bug?  Is there a workaround?

Any help appreciated.

JMarc

