  It's a LMS (Laser Magnetic Something 8-) drive, which is part of (or partly
owned by, I forget) Philips.

  It is a LMS-proprietary interface found on the RRD50 and RRD40 drives. The
2 DEC controllers are the KRP50 (for ISA bus PC's) and the KRQ50 (that's a
guess, but it's a Q-bus host adapter). Both controllers support two drives
via 15-pin D-series connectors.

  DEC did make a SCSI converter for the RRD40 so it could be used in the
Infoserver product line. Unfortunately, I don't know the model number of
this converter.

  In any event, these drives (RRD50/RRD40) are slower than 1x drives, have
an oddball interface, and use screwey caddies (RRD40) which are a real PITA.

