Since you don't know what it is, how do you know what it's worth :-)

|>   Model number : VS31V-A2
|>   SN ab823000FT2 FTZ C232/87 

VS31V-A2 suggests that this is a VAXstation 3200 or a VAXstation 3500. 
The difference is in the size of the cab (and maybe whether it came with RD
or RA drives).

|>   2 scsi interfaces

If this really does have SCSI then it's almost certainly 3rd party.

|>   4 25 pin (serial) interfaces
|>   2 large connectors with black plastic clips, roughly 50 centronics size
|>   1 switch/connector at rear base labeled DELQA

Are there no identifying labels on the front? Can you describe the system
box and its approximate dimensions?

Assuming it is a VAXstation 3200 or VAXstation 3500 you should be able to
open the box and look at the boards inside. Each of them should have an
identifying number (e.g. M7620 for the CPU if I have guessed the model
correctly). List out the boards and we'll know what you have - this will
make the subsequent troubleshooting less painful.

The monitor connection is usually a small DB9-size or DB15-size connector,
but I've never seen one that is centronics-50-way sized. That is more likely 
to be a connector for a CXY asynch comms board or maybe a SCSI card.

Antonio

