Sorry I missed the 8400 6/575 posting. To answer you
question
Sun used 64 CPUs with a DBMS server loading of 82%.

                  Sun       Digital
SD Users          14400     5312
Dialog Steps      4725000   1649000
CPU's	          64        10
DBMS load         82%       95%
Effective CPUs    52.4       9.5
Average response  0.97 secs 1.6 secs		 
time    	

I don't think there is anything in the Sun results to give 
Digital any cause for celebration.

Sun did ~2.9 x the Digital Dialog Steps
        ~2.7 x the Digital Users
	~65% of the Digital response time.

Despite using effectively 52.4 CPUs as opposed 
to effectively 9.5 CPUs Sun acheived a better overall 
SAPs/SPECint ratio than Digital even at the very much 
larger number of CPU's. 

For the number of CPUs used and the DBMS employed 
the 8400 is on the low side in terms of SAPs/SPECint. 
At that sort of throughput a Sun/HP would do ~24
SAPS/SPECint
as opposed to the 18 SAPS/SPECint on the 8400 so somewhere 
you are taking a significant performance hit.

Finally at the very best the current 8400 6/575 should 
be good for another 5% better SD's the E10000 for 18 %

Regards
Andrew Harrison
Enterprise IT Architect



