Total system cost and power consumption also matter.  The 400MHz PPC 
750 is benched on SPECint95 at 17 something, while consuming
only 4.1W/5.?W typical/max.  That is what makes it particularly
suitable for the high performance embedded market, such
as telecom/networking equipment in which multiple CPUs
may be needed in small spaces with restricted air flow.
Current generation Alpha 21164's have power requirements
several times higher, while delivering maybe only 10% more performance 
on SPECint95.





