Leen van Vliet wrote:
>_
>_I've got a DEC100 terminalserver. It has got a 15-pole female connector
>_built in and 8 serial ports.. I know all about the serial ports, but I
>_need to know how I can connect the 15-pole connector with my 15-pole
>_networking-card. Is it 1 on 1 or does the cable have got a special kind
>_of connecting? 
>_I would appreciate some help...

If this is a DECserver 100, it is probably a terminal-server species
that speaks only the LAT protocol, not TCP/IP.

A female AUI Ethernet connector connects to a male AUI connector on
the appropriate device.  You'd probably be better off getting a little
AUI-to-BNC adapter from Allied Telesis and using RG-58 coaxial cable
to connect it to your network, or an AUI-to-UTP adapter (if you can
solve the LAT problem--and I know of no public-domain implementations
of LAT).


>_ I've also got a DEC VT220 color graphical terminal. Does anyone know if
>_ and if so, how I can connect it to a LINUX-server, besides the hardware.

If you have a "color VT220" terminal, it would really be a VT241.
If a VT241 is what you have, the graphics are ReGIS or Sixel. 


Other information on video terminals and connecting them is at

    http://www.cs.utk.edu/~shuford/terminal_index.html

