Hi,

DEC systems are quite flexible with the CDrom drives they will work with (unlike
the SUN systems out there....)

I have used non-DEC badged CDRom drives with my VAX at home without problems.
My CDRom drive is an old 4x Toshiba (50 DM in Germany, second user).

Easy to check if the MAC one will work :
 1. hook it up to the SCSI bus, with all power off,
     internal or external at a free SCSI number.
 2. Power on the system to the >>> promt.
 3. Do a
           ">>> SHOW CONFIG" or
           ">>>SHOW SCSI"
     Whichever you need on the firmware your Alpha is running.

If the CDRom drive is seen by the firmware you should see an entry in the table
and then when you boot the Alpha you should see the CDRom.
Also I have read somewhere that the DEC RRD* drives work fine with the Apple
MACs so it should work the other way round.

Hope this helps.
Have Fun.
John.


